WEBVTT

00:04.314 --> 00:06.942
Man, I love German cars.

00:07.117 --> 00:09.176
If you keep your nose clean
and work hard...

00:09.353 --> 00:12.413
...someday you'll be able
to park them for a living.

00:13.657 --> 00:15.454
Excellent.

00:17.528 --> 00:19.996
Why is my ass getting hot?

00:20.564 --> 00:22.225
You turned on the seat warmer.

00:22.466 --> 00:26.061
Oh, good. I was afraid
I had another case of swamp ass.

00:26.837 --> 00:28.168
Another case?

00:28.372 --> 00:30.533
Yeah, it happens every year
around this time.

00:30.707 --> 00:33.005
Only thing that helps
is aloe vera and Vaseline.

00:33.544 --> 00:36.536
- I see.
- Half a tube of each, right in the crack.

00:37.881 --> 00:41.544
It's like squirting ketchup and mustard
into a hot dog bun.

00:43.053 --> 00:46.079
Then you, like,
mash the sides together.

00:46.256 --> 00:49.453
- Enough.
- Sorry.

00:49.893 --> 00:51.827
You hungry? I'm getting hungry.

00:53.230 --> 00:56.757
I may never eat again. Yellow light.

00:56.967 --> 00:59.333
- I'm slowing down.
- No, no, no. Gun it, gun it.

01:01.905 --> 01:03.770
Man, this thing is a rocket ship.

01:03.974 --> 01:06.534
Okay, okay, now you can slow down.

01:09.112 --> 01:11.046
Should I run for it?

01:11.214 --> 01:14.581
What are you, crazy? Pull over.

01:14.785 --> 01:17.276
You told me to run the light.
My dad's gonna kill me.

01:17.521 --> 01:19.386
Calm down, he's not gonna kill you.

01:19.590 --> 01:23.458
How can I calm down? I just got
my license and now I'm gonna lose it.

01:23.627 --> 01:26.095
All right, all right.
Switch places with me.

01:26.263 --> 01:28.493
- What?
- Just do it.

01:30.601 --> 01:33.934
- And give me your hat.
- You want my lucky hat?

01:34.137 --> 01:37.231
Yeah, I wanna share
in your good fortune.

01:43.380 --> 01:45.371
Good evening, officer.

02:17.280 --> 02:19.043
Hey, where have you guys been?

02:19.616 --> 02:20.776
Van Nuys.

02:21.318 --> 02:24.754
- What were you doing in Van Nuys?
- That's where the jail is.

02:25.689 --> 02:28.317
- What?
- I got arrested.

02:28.525 --> 02:30.152
You're kidding. What for?

02:30.827 --> 02:33.159
Apparently, I ran a red light
at 64 miles an hour.

02:33.330 --> 02:35.457
And I was in the passenger seat.

02:37.034 --> 02:40.800
Yes, I was driving, therefore
you were in the passenger seat.

02:43.707 --> 02:47.006
Anyway, it turns out I had a couple
of unpaid parking tickets.

02:47.177 --> 02:50.874
- Seventeen.
- Thank you.

02:51.081 --> 02:53.072
They arrested you for unpaid tickets?

02:53.483 --> 02:56.782
Well, there was also a bench warrant
when I didn't show up in court.

02:56.987 --> 03:00.354
How could you not show up in court?
Don't they send you a summons?

03:00.524 --> 03:03.652
Lots of them, but I threw them away.

03:05.362 --> 03:07.330
I thought they were for jury duty.

03:08.932 --> 03:11.833
When I didn't show up,
they suspended my license.

03:12.035 --> 03:14.868
And I was in the passenger seat.

03:15.672 --> 03:17.697
You were driving
with a suspended license?

03:18.041 --> 03:20.839
Only for a couple of years.

03:21.945 --> 03:24.880
My license was fine,
so when they took him to the station...

03:25.048 --> 03:26.538
...I followed in the Mercedes.

03:26.950 --> 03:30.113
By the way, I reset all your radio stations
to good stuff.

03:30.887 --> 03:32.514
I'd like to be alone now, Jake.

03:32.723 --> 03:35.351
Understandable.
You've been through a lot.

03:35.525 --> 03:37.789
If you need anyone
to drive you to the movies...

03:37.961 --> 03:40.327
...or the mall, or a strip club,
I'm available.

03:41.198 --> 03:43.860
- Appreciate it.
- You can relax in the passenger seat.

03:44.067 --> 03:45.762
Like I did earlier today.

03:45.969 --> 03:47.527
Get out.

03:50.073 --> 03:52.974
Listen, I am sorry
that you lost your license...

03:53.143 --> 03:55.543
...but I would be remiss
if I did not point out...

03:55.712 --> 03:57.873
...what a bad example
you're setting for Jake.

03:58.081 --> 04:01.380
- Not now, Alan.
- No, I think now is exactly the right time.

04:01.551 --> 04:03.041
That young man looks up to you.

04:03.220 --> 04:05.814
And when he sees you disregard
the rules of the road...

04:05.989 --> 04:08.389
...he's more likely to do it himself.

04:09.626 --> 04:12.925
You're right. You're right. I'm sorry.

04:13.430 --> 04:16.126
Are you really?
Or are you just saying the words?

04:20.737 --> 04:22.932
Don't walk away
when I am talking to you.

04:23.140 --> 04:25.131
- I'm gonna count to three.
- Oh, that's mature.

04:25.308 --> 04:26.366
Three.

04:29.312 --> 04:30.870
Where was one and two?

04:39.256 --> 04:40.655
Hey.

04:40.824 --> 04:42.314
Hey.

04:43.994 --> 04:47.020
You know I was just trying to show
concern for my son.

04:47.264 --> 04:49.926
I do. And you know
I was just trying to cause...

04:50.100 --> 04:52.432
...severe nerve damage
to your shoulder.

04:53.336 --> 04:54.769
I do.

04:56.206 --> 04:58.868
You know, we should maybe come up
with some safe word...

04:59.042 --> 05:01.533
...like "pumpernickel."

05:01.778 --> 05:02.972
Sure, whatever.

05:04.347 --> 05:06.440
You know, until you get
your license back...

05:06.616 --> 05:09.483
...you can count on me to drive you
wherever you need to go.

05:09.653 --> 05:11.120
Thanks.

05:11.288 --> 05:13.882
You know, of course,
during the week I'm working.

05:14.057 --> 05:17.493
- I know.
- Monday nights I'm at the senior center.

05:18.028 --> 05:20.223
What are you doing
at the senior center?

05:20.430 --> 05:22.295
Free Pilates class. Pfft.

05:23.633 --> 05:25.328
They don't even check IDs.

05:27.637 --> 05:30.868
Tuesdays and Thursday nights
they have water aerobics.

05:31.041 --> 05:32.906
Wednesday is low-impact hip-hop...

05:33.076 --> 05:36.341
...and Friday is movie night.

05:36.813 --> 05:38.804
&lt;i>This week is Cocoon.&lt;/i>

05:40.450 --> 05:42.350
Again.

05:43.720 --> 05:46.814
And of course on Saturday, you know,
I need to power down.

05:46.990 --> 05:50.585
And Saturday night, maybe a date.

05:51.761 --> 05:53.956
You're calling those magazines
dates now?

06:00.871 --> 06:03.863
But, hey, any other time you need a ride,
I'm your man.

06:04.040 --> 06:06.941
- Wonderful.
- Sunday is usually good.

06:07.110 --> 06:09.510
- Aha.
- Not this Sunday. I got a little thing.

06:09.713 --> 06:12.546
I know, but what does that
have to do with Sunday?

06:15.518 --> 06:19.420
Cute, cute. Actually, I've been meaning
to talk to you about this...

06:19.589 --> 06:22.558
...but, um, I was waiting for the right time.

06:22.893 --> 06:26.090
Are you moving out?

06:27.397 --> 06:31.026
Ha, ha, ha. No. But that never ceases
to be amusing.

06:32.602 --> 06:35.264
Anyhoo, turns out I was invited...

06:35.438 --> 06:38.430
...to Chelsea's birthday party.
- What?

06:38.608 --> 06:41.202
You know, when she was living here,
we were friends...

06:41.378 --> 06:44.939
...and we've remained friends.
- She invited you to her birthday party?

06:45.148 --> 06:48.413
- I won't go if you don't want me to.
- I don't want you to.

06:48.585 --> 06:51.611
Okay. Asked and answered,
done and done.

06:55.825 --> 06:57.725
I did buy her a lovely scarf.

07:00.163 --> 07:03.155
Will it support your weight
from a shower rod?

07:05.268 --> 07:07.031
Classic.

07:08.038 --> 07:10.836
Of course, it might be a little awkward
if I don't show.

07:11.074 --> 07:13.565
- Why is that?
- I volunteered to bring the ice.

07:13.977 --> 07:17.845
Is that why you've been filling
Ziploc bags with my ice cubes all week?

07:18.181 --> 07:20.809
It's exactly the same ice
as the kind you pay for...

07:20.984 --> 07:23.282
...sans the fancy polar bear label.

07:25.322 --> 07:28.917
I'm not gonna say this again.
Do not hang out with my ex-fiancée.

07:29.125 --> 07:31.787
I hear you. Loud and clear.

07:33.797 --> 07:37.096
It's just so rare I get to socialize
with people my own age.

07:37.300 --> 07:40.030
What, there's no free nookie night
at the senior center?

07:46.376 --> 07:49.777
Okay, what if I just go for cocktails
and skipped dinner?

07:51.381 --> 07:53.349
- Three.
- Three.

07:59.656 --> 08:01.453
- Alan, wake up.
- Pumpernickel!

08:04.227 --> 08:05.956
You gotta go to Chelsea's party.

08:06.663 --> 08:08.221
Uh... Okay.

08:08.398 --> 08:10.832
If you don't,
she's gonna know I told you not to.

08:11.334 --> 08:12.665
That's possible.

08:13.036 --> 08:16.597
It's a sure thing. She knows
you never pass up a free meal.

08:17.240 --> 08:18.867
That's not true.

08:19.042 --> 08:21.602
How many birthdays have you had
at Denny's this year?

08:23.046 --> 08:25.105
All right.

08:25.315 --> 08:26.873
So you gotta go to the party...

08:27.050 --> 08:29.348
...and let her know
I'm doing fine without her.

08:29.552 --> 08:31.383
- Okay.
- But you gotta be cool about it.

08:31.554 --> 08:32.987
You know, like in passing.

08:33.189 --> 08:35.054
Sure, sure. How's this?

08:35.225 --> 08:38.524
Hey, Chelsea, happy birthday.
Charlie's doing fine without you...

08:38.695 --> 08:43.189
...and never wanders around the house
in the middle of the night with a drink.

08:43.366 --> 08:44.492
- Alan?
- Yeah?

08:44.868 --> 08:46.836
You need teeth to say "pumpernickel."

08:48.538 --> 08:50.130
Got it.

08:59.416 --> 09:02.044
Oh. Alan, hi.

09:02.252 --> 09:05.187
I hope I'm not here early.
The invite said 8.

09:05.388 --> 09:09.017
And, uh, 8 it is.

09:09.192 --> 09:10.523
Come on in.

09:12.896 --> 09:14.921
Who is this?

09:15.098 --> 09:17.692
That's how you greet a guest?
"Who is this?"

09:18.268 --> 09:22.466
Okay. Who are you and what the hell
you doing here so freaking early?

09:22.672 --> 09:25.470
This is Alan, Charlie's brother.

09:25.875 --> 09:29.242
Oh. Alan, I'm Ed. Heard a lot about you.

09:29.446 --> 09:31.073
Heard a lot about you too.

09:31.247 --> 09:34.546
You know, you being in the Navy
with Tom...

09:34.751 --> 09:39.211
...and you guys keeping in touch
even though you were both married...

09:39.389 --> 09:41.789
...and now you're reunited. Heh, heh.

09:42.125 --> 09:43.922
Great song.

09:44.094 --> 09:47.427
&lt;i>Reunited and it feels so good&lt;/i>

09:51.301 --> 09:53.735
So where's the birthday girl?

09:53.903 --> 09:55.234
Taking a shower.

09:55.438 --> 09:58.100
Women, huh? Always running late.
Heh, heh.

09:58.274 --> 09:59.571
Bet you don't miss that.

10:01.578 --> 10:03.205
I bought the ice.

10:03.379 --> 10:04.505
Oh!

10:06.216 --> 10:09.583
I guess the bottom got wet.
You know how that is.

10:09.786 --> 10:12.778
Because it happens to everybody,
not because you're gay.

10:13.656 --> 10:16.318
And I thought you were exaggerating.

10:17.160 --> 10:20.254
And remember, lookie, no touchee.

10:27.837 --> 10:30.806
- What's that?
- A birthday present for Chelsea.

10:31.007 --> 10:32.634
But you guys broke up.

10:32.809 --> 10:35.107
Yeah, well, I bought it
a couple of months ago.

10:35.311 --> 10:38.337
- Why?
- I thought that's when her birthday was.

10:40.283 --> 10:43.184
Turns out I confused it
with St. Patrick's Day.

10:43.887 --> 10:45.047
Are those real diamonds?

10:45.788 --> 10:47.619
- Yep.
- Burn.

10:48.958 --> 10:49.982
What?

10:50.160 --> 10:52.890
You could have saved a lot of money
with Cuban zirconium.

10:54.864 --> 10:56.661
"Cuban" zirconium?

10:57.333 --> 11:00.461
Yeah. Girls can't tell because
it's just as sparkly as a diamond...

11:00.637 --> 11:03.299
...and it's cheap
because it's from Cuba.

11:06.643 --> 11:08.167
Good Lord, you're an idiot.

11:09.145 --> 11:12.581
I'm not the one who wasted money on
a bracelet for a girl who dumped me.

11:12.815 --> 11:15.716
It's not a waste.
I'm still gonna give it to her.

11:19.155 --> 11:22.181
In fact, come on,
you're driving me to Chelsea's.

11:22.358 --> 11:24.417
Did it occur to you
that I might have plans?

11:25.361 --> 11:27.522
Oh, I'm sorry. Do you have plans?

11:27.730 --> 11:29.527
No, but there's a principle involved.

11:31.334 --> 11:34.394
I'm just saying, there's a right way
and there's a wrong way.

11:40.410 --> 11:41.707
You need any condoms?

11:41.878 --> 11:44.073
- No. Do you?
- No. I got a buttload.

11:45.748 --> 11:49.707
A buttload, huh? You may need to read
the instructions more carefully.

11:50.587 --> 11:51.952
I don't get it.

11:53.489 --> 11:57.323
Wait, wait, wait.
Have you used any of them yet?

11:57.560 --> 11:59.824
- Yeah, sure.
- For sex?

12:00.563 --> 12:02.030
Oh. Um...

12:02.198 --> 12:04.223
No. For water balloons.

12:05.068 --> 12:08.902
Well, keep a few in reserve
because you're not really breeding stock.

12:10.473 --> 12:14.239
- So, what are you looking for?
- A birthday card for Chelsea.

12:14.410 --> 12:15.900
Good idea.

12:17.680 --> 12:20.740
Ha. Look at this one.
It says, "I got you a birthday package."

12:20.917 --> 12:25.217
On the inside, it's a naked fat guy with
a hole for you to pop your finger through.

12:25.655 --> 12:27.782
- Mm, no.
- Are you sure?

12:27.957 --> 12:30.289
He really likes you.

12:36.966 --> 12:38.661
Here we go.

12:39.302 --> 12:42.499
"Wishing you the dreams of your heart,
all the love in the world...

12:42.672 --> 12:45.334
...and the beautiful day
you deserve for being special."

12:45.541 --> 12:47.270
That's not funny.

12:47.944 --> 12:49.434
It's not supposed to be funny.

12:49.612 --> 12:51.978
Yeah, well, mission accomplished.

12:53.816 --> 12:58.116
Ha. Look at this one. It's an old lady with
banana boobs and a dog looking at her.

12:58.288 --> 13:00.620
Inside it says,
"How many were in your litter?"

13:01.057 --> 13:02.615
That's not a birthday card.

13:02.825 --> 13:05.385
It could be.
Write "happy birthday" inside.

13:06.696 --> 13:08.459
I need a real birthday card.

13:08.831 --> 13:10.264
Okay.

13:11.467 --> 13:13.560
Here's one with a puppy on it.

13:14.404 --> 13:17.339
"For someone very special
on her birthday.

13:17.507 --> 13:20.965
Each day is a beautiful gift to enjoy."
That's pretty good.

13:21.177 --> 13:22.735
And then you could cut a hole...

13:22.912 --> 13:25.847
...and pop your pinkie through
and give that dog a bone.

13:29.085 --> 13:31.849
I can't help you
if you're not gonna work with me.

13:36.292 --> 13:38.317
I'm really glad you came, Alan.

13:38.528 --> 13:42.089
How could I not? We're friends.

13:42.332 --> 13:45.233
I know, but I was afraid
it might be uncomfortable for you.

13:45.401 --> 13:47.562
No, no, don't be silly.

13:48.237 --> 13:51.832
So that's it?
No dinner, just finger foods?

13:52.842 --> 13:54.673
- Sorry.
- Oh, no, it's fine.

13:54.844 --> 13:57.711
I can never have enough
prosciutto and melon.

13:57.880 --> 14:00.348
Hey, that'd be a good name
for a singing act.

14:00.550 --> 14:02.541
Prosciutto and Melon. Heh, heh.

14:02.719 --> 14:07.452
Ladies and gentlemen, the song stylings
of Prosciutto and Melon.

14:10.126 --> 14:13.425
There's an open mike night
at the senior center. I'm gonna use that.

14:14.364 --> 14:16.355
Terrific.

14:16.699 --> 14:18.428
- So how's he doing?
- Who?

14:18.835 --> 14:21.099
- Alan.
- Oh, Charlie?

14:21.270 --> 14:22.897
He's doing fine. Just fine.

14:23.106 --> 14:25.131
Good, good.

14:25.775 --> 14:28.437
In fact, he told me to tell you
happy birthday.

14:28.611 --> 14:30.579
Oh, that's nice. Tell him I said thanks.

14:30.780 --> 14:34.045
I will. And I'm sure
he'd say, you're welcome.

14:38.154 --> 14:42.147
So how are you doing?
And it's me asking, not Charlie.

14:42.358 --> 14:45.885
I'm sure he'd be interested. Not that
I'd tell him, unless you want me to.

14:46.062 --> 14:50.226
Do you want me to? Tell me how you're
doing first and then we can decide.

14:51.401 --> 14:55.735
- I'm doing fine, Alan.
- Good, good. So's Charlie. Heh, heh.

14:55.905 --> 14:57.338
Can we change the subject?

14:57.507 --> 15:00.135
You're the one who brought it up,
but sure.

15:04.280 --> 15:07.272
You ever think about
your dad and Ed having sex?

15:09.652 --> 15:12.917
"Happy birthday, thinking of you."

15:13.623 --> 15:14.783
What's wrong with it?

15:14.991 --> 15:17.323
It's, what do you call it? Redumbnent.

15:18.628 --> 15:19.788
"Redumbnent"?

15:19.996 --> 15:23.329
Yeah. You got her a present
and you got her a birthday card.

15:23.499 --> 15:28.095
You're obviously thinking of her. Saying
you're thinking of her is redumbnent.

15:28.504 --> 15:33.271
So if you act like a moron, saying
you're a moron would be redumbnent.

15:33.476 --> 15:34.602
Now you're getting it.

15:35.411 --> 15:39.006
Oh, buddy, you really shouldn't be
walking around without a helmet.

15:39.615 --> 15:42.641
- Wait here, I'll be right back.
- Why can't I go with you?

15:42.819 --> 15:45.845
Because I'm just gonna give Chelsea
the bracelet and leave.

15:46.022 --> 15:50.652
Bring me back a piece of cake.
Corner with a flower would be nice.

16:14.383 --> 16:17.784
- What the hell are you doing?
- Uh...

16:17.954 --> 16:19.888
Checking for leaks?

16:22.258 --> 16:23.850
Listen...

16:25.962 --> 16:28.556
...I need you to go up
and give Chelsea the present.

16:28.731 --> 16:29.993
Why? Did you wuss out?

16:30.366 --> 16:32.834
No, no.
I just don't wanna make a scene.

16:33.035 --> 16:34.662
Here, wuss, wuss, wuss.

16:34.871 --> 16:35.997
Wuss, wuss, wuss.

16:36.472 --> 16:38.770
Wuss, wuss.

16:40.343 --> 16:42.868
Just take the bracelet,
ring the doorbell, say:

16:43.045 --> 16:45.707
"Happy birthday. This is from
Uncle Charlie," and leave.

16:45.882 --> 16:47.110
Can I get a piece of cake?

16:47.350 --> 16:48.908
Fine. Grab a piece of cake.

16:49.118 --> 16:51.382
If they haven't cut the cake,
can I hang out?

16:51.787 --> 16:53.846
No. I'm not gonna sit here
waiting for you.

16:54.056 --> 16:57.184
You don't really have a choice.
You're not allowed to drive.

16:57.927 --> 16:59.019
What are you saying?

16:59.228 --> 17:03.096
Well, at the risk of being redumbnent,
I'm saying I'll be having cake.

17:06.269 --> 17:09.602
I can't believe I'm being blackmailed
by Forrest Gump.

17:10.506 --> 17:12.599
Should I tell her
you're waiting out here?

17:12.775 --> 17:14.242
No. Are you nuts?

17:14.443 --> 17:17.606
I was thinking it'd be a good way
to get a second piece of cake.

17:17.780 --> 17:19.213
Get out of here.

17:21.551 --> 17:24.452
Run, Forrest, run.

17:25.321 --> 17:28.449
What if I meet a cute girl up there?
Would you mind walking home?

17:28.624 --> 17:31.923
Jake, I swear to God,
do not make me get out of this car.

17:32.128 --> 17:34.961
Excuse me, let's not forget
who's doing who a favor here.

17:37.967 --> 17:39.457
Go.

17:39.669 --> 17:41.432
Yes, sir.

17:45.908 --> 17:48.138
"Extra large"? Pfft.

17:48.311 --> 17:51.838
Yeah, maybe if he wears it
as a lucky hat.

17:54.650 --> 17:57.983
So, what about the blond?
Is she single?

17:58.154 --> 18:00.418
Yeah. She's a little crazy.

18:00.590 --> 18:04.686
Not a deal breaker. The well-adjusted
ones generally won't come near me.

18:05.695 --> 18:06.753
Hey, Dad.

18:07.930 --> 18:09.363
What are you doing here?

18:09.599 --> 18:12.159
Uncle Charlie wanted me to give
Chelsea this present.

18:12.368 --> 18:15.064
Here. So have you cut the cake yet?

18:16.973 --> 18:19.134
- No.
- We haven't sung "Happy Birthday" yet.

18:19.308 --> 18:20.502
Oh.

18:20.676 --> 18:24.772
&lt;i>Happy birthday to you&lt;/i>

18:25.314 --> 18:28.806
&lt;i>Happy birthday to you&lt;/i>

18:29.652 --> 18:34.453
&lt;i>Happy birthday dear Chelsea&lt;/i>

18:35.291 --> 18:39.489
&lt;i>Happy birthday to you&lt;/i>

18:44.100 --> 18:46.625
Thank you. Thank you for coming.

18:46.802 --> 18:49.396
Excuse me, I need to get some air.

18:51.007 --> 18:54.340
Wasn't me. I always claim them,
you know that.

18:54.543 --> 18:56.238
Come on, Skipper.

18:59.815 --> 19:00.839
So where's the cake?

19:25.741 --> 19:27.368
Ah, jeez.

19:44.894 --> 19:48.660
Oh, this is not gonna end well.

19:54.070 --> 19:55.367
Charlie?

19:56.305 --> 20:00.264
Hey, Chels. Happy birthday.

20:09.085 --> 20:12.213
Uncle Charlie's gonna pay me
to drive him back and forth to work?

20:12.388 --> 20:14.049
Oh, that's nice.

20:14.223 --> 20:16.054
I'm ready.

20:22.364 --> 20:25.265
I get to drive his car twice a day
for three to six months...

20:25.434 --> 20:28.767
...depending on good behavior.
Move it, numb nuts.

20:29.238 --> 20:31.433
Smart money's on six.
